                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "39666559",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198061931630",
                            "num_reviews": 71,
                            "playtime_forever": 52,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 52,
                            "last_played": 1517006478
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I absolutely love the kefling games and I absolutely understand why they designed it the way they did, In some ways it feels just like a kefling game. but as of right now, it doesn't look like it has very much meat to it. The controls are weird, they try to give you some ghost hand but it just ends up being a glitchy mess more times than not, in my opinion, it would probably be best to get rid of the ghost hand and just keep it on the harvesting animation. maybe add a destroying animation because I've accidently destroyed buildings because of how fidgety the ghost hand is. The graphics are find but it kind of looks a little strange through my vive, no options to adjust anything. and my biggest peeve is that you don't really feel like a Giant. I just feel like I'm playing tabletop simulator. I remember playing Kefling on xbox when you could be your avatar, there was so much sense of exploration, but this game is kind of dissapointing. It's not worth $15 in my opinion, nor the $20 it will be normally. I wouldn't recomend until further updated.",
